# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/octo-t8 four-card DEVELOPMENT window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/octo-t8 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-octo-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the branch. The device pieces of serving_octo.DEVICE_PIECES are BUILT on the host and tested
# on CPU; none of them has run on a card, and the admission logs every card question as an '[OCTO] UNQUALIFIED' line (serving_octo.UNQUALIFIED_ITEMS, each naming the job that settles it).
# Substitute the placeholder in every template with one command (sed -i 's/tp4-octo-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every
# template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.

# M1 (MEMORY at EIGHT LIVE, the pool lowered to 16,500 blocks and the trace region raised to 640 MiB): the gate's memory plan on the timed octo arm: eight users, each at the largest admitted prompt. READ: the DRAM ledger after every engine build and at the end; the floor and the largest free block
# per chip; the trace region's largest free block at 8 live. Pass (the seats8 bars): free DRAM at 8 live at least 3 GB per chip, the floor at least 1 GB, the trace region's largest free block at least 44 MB, and the free reading no more than 0.2 GB below the parent's (M0 below). Stop rule: below the bars.

C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-octo-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-octo
C2_GATE_PLAN=memory
C2_GATE_JIT=record
